A||N||3||MontanaFiero||Removing the Fastback Clip...am I missing a bolt?||||1||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||10-01-2001||11:11 AM||||Can anyone tell me if theFastback Clip has a bolt behind the Sail Panels like the Notchback Clip does??<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||10-01-2001||11:47 AM||||There is a bolt in each B pillar. THe B pillar is where the rear speakers are located. If I remember the bolt is slightly above the hole opening so you have to look carefully. Oh and be careful when you stick your socket on an extension through the hole because it is easy to knock the socket off while withdrawing it and the socket will fall off the face of the earth, never to be seen again.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||10-01-2001||12:17 PM||||On the Notchback, there is also a bolt behind the sail panels, requiring the removal of the sail panels to get to it. I am just wondering if this one exists on the fastback, since the sail panels are so difficult to remove.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-01-2001||01:26 PM||||No need to remove EITHER fastback sails OR coupe sails if still factory stuff!<BR>Held on by stamped nuts in most cases. After being removed, just spread apart to dislodge through bolts.||||reg||1
